      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another regimen**, such as extended-release dosing\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it."
      }
